WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.048 --> 00:00:02.760
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:04.390
- [Joanna] Five monitors to test,

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:06.840
including the new Apple Studio Display,

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.713
all concealed so we don't
know which is which.

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:12.160
Two sets of eyes.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.760
One pair belonging to a
professional colorist.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.780
- So this one is a thumbs up.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.100
Here come the horses.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.253
Good temporal motion.

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:21.920
- Honestly, I feel like
I'm at an eye doctor.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.700
I have zero idea what this test does.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:27.690
One, okay, maybe two winning monitors.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.990
Welcome to Monitor Madness,

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:31.730
AKA the only way to determine

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:35.400
if Apple's new Studio Display
is worth your hard-earned.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.810
- [Man] 1,599.

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:39.231
- Ah yes, $1,600.

00:00:39.231 --> 00:00:40.640
Sorry, I mean.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.870
- [Man] 1,599.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:43.390
- For a monitor.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:47.010
Two years ago, I bought
this LG monitor for $450

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.400
and I thought that was a
lot of money for a monitor.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.840
But the Apple Studio monitor

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:53.540
isn't just a boring old computer monitor.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:55.200
It's a smart monitor.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.060
Inside, it's got an A13 bionic chip,

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:00.410
the same one that's in the iPhone 11.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:01.243
For real.

00:01:01.243 --> 00:01:03.410
That processor unlocks
better video calling

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:04.833
and speaker performance

00:01:04.833 --> 00:01:07.000
or at least, that's what Apple says.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.520
But just how good is it

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.560
and what makes one monitor more expensive

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:11.820
than another monitor?

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:14.650
To find out, I put the
27-inch Studio Display

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:17.050
up against four other monitors.

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:18.930
A 5K LG display,

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:21.450
which has basically the
same specs as the Studio

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.960
and costs $300 less.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:26.520
My own 4K LG monitor.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.330
And to round out the comparison,

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:32.090
a $370 4K Samsung smart monitor,

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:34.060
and a professional 4K Dell

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:37.320
that costs nearly $4,000.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.260
If you want the names the
confusing monitor numbers,

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:41.880
take a screenshot of this.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.930
I'm not saying them out loud.

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:45.020
Here we go.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:46.063
Monitor testing.

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:48.360
We're actually not going anywhere.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.040
We're staying in the studio

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:54.080
'cause Mac Studio Display and studio.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.963
Number one, display quality.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:58.400
Here's the thing about testing this.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.540
To my eye, displays have gotten so good

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.820
that it's actually hard
to tell the difference.

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:05.100
The best way you can tell the crispness

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:08.030
of this is in Ed Harris' wrinkles.

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:10.890
That's why I brought in someone
with better eyes than me.

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:13.870
Daniel Silverman is a
professional colorist.

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:15.630
He spends his days color correcting

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:17.600
movies and advertisements.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.310
So he has a great eye for this stuff.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:23.000
My producer Kenny hid the
five different displays

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.740
and hooked them up to the
new Mac Studio desktop,

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:27.010
which had test files,

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:28.820
including 4K videos.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:30.640
Yes, the "Top Gun" trailer.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.270
And some professional color test tools.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:34.480
The Studio Display, by the way,

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:38.500
works with any newer Mac,
not just this new desktop.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:40.300
- Yeah, the whites look pretty good.

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:42.710
Grays look pretty good.

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:44.940
- [Joanna] Dan and I both
evaluated them on our own

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:47.030
so not to influence each other.

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:50.460
Out of them all, Dan liked
both the LG displays the best,

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:52.710
specifically the more expensive one.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:54.300
- All of the first three so far.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.400
This one seems pretty good.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.000
There's good detail.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.990
There's no clipping, there's no crushing.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:04.240
- I liked the Apple Studio
and the 5K LG the best

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:07.120
and really struggled to tell
the difference between them.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.570
I mean, honestly, if you told me

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:11.200
that this display and the
last one were the same,

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.640
I kind of would believe you.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:16.350
Maybe the like coloring here

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:18.670
is a little bit yellower.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:21.370
I need to look at these side by side.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:24.200
We both noticed a yellowish
tint on the Apple Display

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.730
but when we turned off True Tone,

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:27.630
Apple's automatic adjustment feature,

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:30.580
any noticeable color
irregularity was gone.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:32.560
- Oh, that's it, it's much less yellow.

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:33.660
It still looks different

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:36.920
but I think the LG is
almost like a touch cooler.

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:38.620
And honestly, like between these two,

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:41.700
they're pretty excellent looking monitors.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.220
- So yeah, tie on display quality.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:46.093
Number two, webcam quality.

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:49.030
Sitting at the top of Apple's display

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:51.230
is a 12-megapixel camera.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.570
But how is the image quality?

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:54.610
Not good.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:56.750
Actually, bad.

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:57.650
Let's take a look.

00:03:57.650 --> 00:03:59.200
Here's the Apple Studio Display

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.760
in my well-lit home office.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:02.810
Grainy.

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:05.150
Now look at it compared
to the front-facing camera

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:06.960
on the iPhone 11 Pro,

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:10.660
which has the same A13
processor and camera.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:12.480
Even the 14-inch MacBook Pro

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.920
and the 5K LG monitor's
webcam looked better.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:18.010
Same situation in the studio.

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:18.950
Oof.

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:21.070
It just consistently produced grainy

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:24.440
and washed-out images,
even in good lighting.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:25.817
An Apple spokeswoman told me,

00:04:25.817 --> 00:04:27.810
"We discovered an issue where the system

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:29.860
is not behaving as expected.

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:32.980
We'll be making improvements
in a future software update."

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:34.550
But here's the coolest feature.

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:36.160
It's called Center Stage

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.350
and as I move around,
the webcam moves around.

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:41.280
And it pans to wherever I go.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.820
This is very fun.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:44.380
Go, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.140
Oh, you get me down here.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:47.973
Number three, speaker quality.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:51.330
There are six speakers in the Display

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:53.430
and boy are they good.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:54.880
Now for the spatial audio test

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:56.800
where I play music that we
don't have the rights to

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.000
so you won't be bale to listen to it.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.667
(playful music)

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:06.300
Yes, the A13 chip also
enables spatial audio,

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.900
a virtual surround sound experience.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:10.710
Either way, these speakers crushed

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.820
every other monitor's built-in speakers

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:14.543
in my side-by-side tests.

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:17.483
Number four, other things.

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:20.780
Finally, a monitor isn't
just a monitor anymore

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:22.100
if you have a laptop.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:23.840
It's a docking station.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:25.820
The Studio has this one Thunderbolt port,

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:27.950
capable of fast charging a laptop,

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:30.200
and then three other USB-C ports

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.430
that can be used as a
hub for your other gear

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:35.550
so you don't always have to
plug them into your laptop.

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:38.890
The 5K LG has a similar
selection of ports.

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:42.550
My own 4K LG has a
selection of older ports.

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:45.020
But you know what both of those LGs have?

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:46.940
Adjustable stands.

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:50.450
The Studio Display requires
you pay an extra $400

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.300
for a height adjustment stand

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:55.407
or you know, you could
just pull this pro move.

00:05:55.407 --> 00:05:57.060
(books stacking)

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:58.640
So what do you do?

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:00.850
Well, if you don't care
about speaker quality

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:02.760
or an attractive aluminum design,

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:06.460
save the $300 and get the 5K LG.

00:06:06.460 --> 00:06:08.170
But here's some bad news.

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:10.840
The LG is sold out now
at various retailers

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:12.270
but an LG spokesman told me

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:14.220
that it's still an active product.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:17.650
He expects it to be back
in stock in early April.

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:19.320
But honestly, I wasn't blown away enough

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:21.890
to buy either of these 5K monitors.

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:24.950
Maybe that will change with
this webcam software update

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:27.220
but right now, Apple's
perks aren't good enough

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:31.820
to make me give up my
trusty $450 LG 4K display,

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:34.533
which let me remind you does this.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.890
Better luck next time in
Monitor Madness, Apple.

